        {
          "id": "85728e38-4db0-32bc-8f4c-b080eb5fe409",
          "content": {
            "id": "85728e38-4db0-32bc-8f4c-b080eb5fe409",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Sinclair ends Kimmel boycott: What this illustrates about linear TV",
            "description": "<p>Sinclair Broadcast Group (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/SBGI\">SBGI</a>) ended its boycott of ABC's <em>Jimmy Kimmel Live! </em>on Friday after the titular late night host returned from his suspension on Tuesday. Earlier this week, the broadcast company <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/nexstar-joins-sinclair-jimmy-kimmel-161004113.html\">teamed with Nexstar Media Group</a> (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/NXST\">NXST</a>) to air news over the show on their local stations.</p>\n<p>Yahoo Finance senior media reporter <a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/author/alexandra-canal/?.tsrc=fin-srch\">Allie Canal</a> highlights <a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/how-disneys-kimmel-controversy-highlights-linear-tvs-fragility-190413148.html\">linear TV's fragility</a> in this case of broadcaster backlash. LightShed Partners media analyst Rich Greenfield made the case to Yahoo Finance as to why Disney (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/DIS\">DIS</a>) c<a data-i13n=\"cpos:7;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/disney-spin-off-abc-over-172500936.html\">ould spin-off ABC.</a></p>\n<p>Hear why Needham & Company's Laura Martin thinks Disney <a data-i13n=\"cpos:8;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/disney-shut-down-abc-analyst-213036821.html\">should just shut down ABC</a> in an interview with Yahoo Finance earlier this week.</p>\n<p>Plex CEO Keith Valory also commented that media companies have <a data-i13n=\"cpos:9;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/media-companies-moral-obligation-uphold-152443132.html\">a \"moral obligation\" to uphold free speech practices</a> against government pressures.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:10;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-domination/\">Market Domination</a>.</p>",
            "summary": "Sinclair Broadcast Group (SBGI) ended its boycott of ABC's Jimmy Kimmel Live! on Friday after the titular late night host returned from his suspension on Tuesday. Earlier this week, the broadcast company teamed with Nexstar Media Group (NXST) to air news over the show on their local stations. Yahoo Finance senior media reporter Allie Canal highlights linear TV's fragility in this case of broadcaster backlash. LightShed Partners media analyst Rich Greenfield made the case to Yahoo Finance as to why Disney (DIS) could spin-off ABC. Hear why Needham & Company's Laura Martin thinks Disney should just shut down ABC in an interview with Yahoo Finance earlier this week. Plex CEO Keith Valory also commented that media companies have a \"moral obligation\" to uphold free speech practices against government pressures. To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more&nbsp;Market Domination.",
