          "content": {
            "id": "8f65a782-ba6f-3430-b649-e92515f515a7",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Jimmy Kimmel returns on ABC: What it means for stocks",
            "description": "<p>In his first show on ABC since being suspended over his comments on Charlie Kirk's assassination, Jimmy Kimmel apologized for \"making light\" of the subject.</p>\n<p>As Sinclair (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/SBGI\">SBGI</a>) and Nextstar (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/NXST\">NXST</a>) decided not to resume broadcasting the comedian, Ramzan Karmali looks at the business implications of the controversy, which comes at a time when ABC parent Disney (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/DIS\">DIS</a>) is raising prices to boost profitability after years of heavy investment.</p>\n<p>For more live coverage of markets watch the full episode of<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cLr6hc2-oMY&list=PLx28zU8ctIRqTE7Y4uXTY-S2oHlwDsL5c\"> Market Sunrise</a> and head to<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/\"> Yahoo Finance</a>.</p>",
            "summary": "In his first show on ABC since being suspended over his comments on Charlie Kirk's assassination, Jimmy Kimmel apologized for \"making light\" of the subject. As Sinclair (SBGI) and Nextstar (NXST) decided not to resume broadcasting the comedian, Ramzan Karmali looks at the business implications of the controversy, which comes at a time when ABC parent Disney (DIS) is raising prices to boost profitability after years of heavy investment. For more live coverage of markets watch the full episode of Market Sunrise and head to Yahoo Finance.",
